00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,614
Sustainable cadence beats heroic weeks that collapse.

2
00:00:02,614 --> 00:00:04,854
This lesson is about burnout prevention.

3
00:00:04,854 --> 00:00:05,601
Sustainable cadence.

4
00:00:05,601 --> 00:00:08,214
Do not treat this as theory only.

5
00:00:08,214 --> 00:00:11,948
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

6
00:00:11,948 --> 00:00:17,548
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

7
00:00:17,548 --> 00:00:21,656
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

8
00:00:21,656 --> 00:00:26,136
Stay practical: set a stop rule before you optimize branding or tools.

9
00:00:26,456 --> 00:00:31,552
Set a stop rule: max deep blocks per day, and a hard end time.

10
00:00:31,552 --> 00:00:34,100
Remember the objective: set a stop rule.

11
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:38,104
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

12
00:00:38,104 --> 00:00:42,472
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

13
00:00:42,472 --> 00:00:46,476
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

14
00:00:46,476 --> 00:00:50,844
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

15
00:00:50,844 --> 00:00:53,392
Talk to a real person when possible.

16
00:00:53,392 --> 00:00:54,848
Feedback beats guessing alone.

17
00:00:55,168 --> 00:00:57,847
Protect sleep and one recovery block weekly.

